WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.202
Who's the best player you've
had to play against in general?

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.436
- Aaron Rodgers.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.138
- Please talk about that.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.339
- Oh, man.
He's phenomenal.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.707
I remember——I could
tell you one play.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:10.410
We had a practice squad guy 
lined up on 17, right?
- Right.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.746
- So I'm disguising them
kind of down towards the box

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.247
but I'm actually going back.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.549
So, for some reason,
I'm in this stance

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.018
and I'm never in this stance.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:19.886
A-Rod looked at me and smiled

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.454
and kinda gave,
like, a lil' giggle.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:24.724
And then did something
with his hand to 17.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.326
I knew it was a signal to 17.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:29.162
I looked at 17, I looked
at my guy that's covering him.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.464
I said, "S--t."

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.999
As soon as he said "Hut"

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.934
I tried to run
before he said "Hut."

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.270
He already said it.
I'm already out of leverage.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.105
Touchdown to 17 over my guy.
- Man.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:39.172
Touchdown to 17 over my guy.
- Man.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:43.476
- So just the mindset,
his preparation for the game

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.744
his ability to move out
of the pocket

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:45.812
and throw off his back foot.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:46.913
You never see any
quarterbacks here

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.281
besides, I think, Brett Favre

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.416
throw off his back foot
like he does.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.317
- Right, right.
- And he's just a great guy.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.419
- Right, right.
- And he's just a great guy.

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:52.719
- Right, right.
- And he's just a great guy.

